.TH INPUT-BOOST 8 "2026-11-10" "gnome-phone 0.1.0" "GNOME Phone"
.SH NAME
input-boost \- GPU clock floor while the touchscreen is touched
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B input-boost
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the input devices (without grabbing them) and, while a finger is on the touchscreen and for a moment after, raises the minimum frequency of the GPU's devfreq (and optionally of CPU frequency policies), as Android's input boost does. It runs as input-boost.service, which is not enabled on installation: the floor must suit the device.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INPUT_BOOST_GPU
The GPU's devfreq directory (default: the first /sys/class/devfreq/*.gpu).
.TP
.B INPUT_BOOST_GPU_HZ
Its floor while boosted, in Hz (default 572000000).
.TP
.B INPUT_BOOST_CPU
CPU floors while boosted, as "policy0=1300000 policy4=1066000" (kHz; default none).
.TP
.B INPUT_BOOST_HOLD_MS
How long the boost outlasts the last event (default 1200).
.SH SEE ALSO
systemd.exec(5)
